  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "Findings reflect user dynamics on a single social platform during one localized fire event.",
      "what": "The authors analyzed all sociopolitical Bluesky posts regarding the January 2025 Los Angeles wildfire to measure how distance from the event shaped online activity. Local and international users showed higher rates of collective action participation compared to regional and national users. Conversely, attention concentrated among regional and national accounts, which engaged primarily in viral, non-participatory political talk.",
      "why": "It identifies a spatial mismatch in digital crisis communication, showing that online attention concentrates among users least likely to engage in direct collective action."
    }
